nt_sha256":"sha256:9d7ac9e4b17faff9b764338a23a0a316e138827fd74387aa8a51347e2ccf3d70","file":"preprints/Global-quantum-geometric-Langlands-at-irrational-level-October-4-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":28,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"e120b83119422b4e24f03a65f9dc0cd048b97bbdaeefd04c1e71bf64d690e207","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Global-quantum-geometric-Langlands-at-irrational-level-October-4-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:9d7ac9e4b17faff9b764338a23a0a316e138827fd74387aa8a51347e2ccf3d70","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Global-quantum-geometric-Langlands-at-irrational-level-October-4-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L28"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every $c\\in\\mathbb C\\setminus\\mathbb Q$ there is an equivalence of\npresentable $\\mathbb C$-linear DG categories\n\\begin{equation}\\label{intro:equivalence}\n  D_c(\\operatorname{Bun}_G(X))\n    \\simeq\n  D_{-1/(rc)}(\\operatorname{Bun}_{G^\\vee}(X)).\n\\end{equation}\nThe construction uses the given global forms and all connected components.\nIt is characterized by the localization--Whittaker comparison of\nSection~\\ref{sec:equivalence}, including its compatibility with families of\nmarked points and their collisions. It also intertwines central torsor actions\nwith the corresponding transgression local systems."}
